      "content": "i get that it might look like a misunderstanding from the outside, but some people argue that even if it isn't the *stated* goal, the actual policies—like congestion pricing or removing parking to make things more walkable—feel like a slow way of forcing people out of their cars and limiting their freedom. isn't there a valid way to look at this as a critique of government overreach, even if you don't believe the extreme stuff?",
